    <dc:description>
        The Sinews of Peace, often referred to as the Iron Curtain speech, was delivered by Winston Churchill on 5 March 1946,
        at Westminster College in Fulton, Missouri. In this speech, Churchill warned against the expansionist policies of the
        Soviet Union and advocated for a strong alliance between Western nations to counter the threat of communism.
    </dc:description>

